=== HINT 1: safe_divide ===
__try {
    result = a / b;
}
__except(GetExceptionCode() == EXCEPTION_INT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO
         ? EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER : EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH) {
    return INT_MIN;
}

=== HINT 2: Filter values ===
EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER   (1)  - execute the __except block (catch)
EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH   (0)  - don't handle here, unwind further
EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_EXECUTION(-1) - resume at faulting instruction (rare/dangerous)

=== HINT 3: __finally ===
__try {
    // code that might fail
}
__finally {
    cleaned_up = 1;   // ALWAYS runs, even if exception propagates
}
Note: __finally and __except cannot both appear in the same __try block directly.
Nest them: outer __try/__finally, inner __try/__except.

=== HINT 4: Common exception codes ===
EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION        0xC0000005
EXCEPTION_INT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO      0xC0000094
EXCEPTION_STACK_OVERFLOW           0xC00000FD
EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT               0x80000003
